1
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:52,537
Make me this time!

2
00:01:52,717 --> 00:01:53,997
Looks like it all worked out.

3
00:01:54,417 --> 00:01:55,077
Seems so.

4
00:01:57,037 --> 00:01:59,757
Now it's time to choose your new crew member!

5
00:02:00,197 --> 00:02:01,937
Who do you want, Straw Hat Luffy?

6
00:02:02,517 --> 00:02:04,477
Come on, Chopper, get over here!

7
00:02:09,657 --> 00:02:11,357
I'll miss you, Choppy!

8
00:02:11,937 --> 00:02:13,357
I was so scared!

9
00:02:13,617 --> 00:02:15,117
I'm so happy you won!

10
00:02:15,777 --> 00:02:16,617
Are you kidding?

11
00:02:16,797 --> 00:02:19,337
A bunch of suckers like that could never beat my crew.

12
00:02:19,337 --> 00:02:22,037
We've seen blood, sweat, and plenty of tears today,

13
00:02:22,157 --> 00:02:24,977
but the Davy Pack fight has finally drawn to a close.

14
00:02:25,237 --> 00:02:28,317
With the Straw Hacks reclaiming their doctor, Tony Tony Chopper,

15
00:02:28,517 --> 00:02:30,177
I say this match ends in a draw!

16
00:02:30,737 --> 00:02:32,877
Hold it! Hold it! Hold it!

17
00:02:33,177 --> 00:02:33,497
Huh?

18
00:02:34,837 --> 00:02:38,957
Any captain worth his way to Seaweed knows there are no draws in the pirate world.

19
00:02:39,237 --> 00:02:40,637
It's plunder or be plunder.

20
00:02:41,217 --> 00:02:43,977
You won't let it end like this, will you?

21
00:02:46,337 --> 00:02:48,717
Wait, is he saying what I think he is?

22
00:02:48,717 --> 00:02:49,937
Come on.

23
00:02:50,377 --> 00:02:54,197
How about another three-coin game to decide which one of us is really the best?

24
00:02:54,917 --> 00:02:56,297
Yeah, like we'd agree to that.

25
00:02:56,437 --> 00:02:59,277
After all that cheating, you'd have to be an idiot to go for another round.

26
00:03:00,717 --> 00:03:03,137
Oh no! Oh no! Oh no no no!

27
00:03:03,397 --> 00:03:04,357
Oh no no no no no!

28
00:03:06,537 --> 00:03:08,057
You're on, split head!

29
00:03:08,057 --> 00:03:10,977
What if we were talking about?

30
00:03:10,977 --> 00:03:12,457
We don't have anything to gain from this!

31
00:03:12,577 --> 00:03:14,377
I don't want any of those losers that I proved!

32
00:03:14,377 --> 00:03:16,457
So I think we'd be better off trading you to them!

33
00:03:16,957 --> 00:03:18,917
Okay, this is the last time.

34
00:03:19,117 --> 00:03:20,977
I won't do it again, I promise.

35
00:03:21,397 --> 00:03:21,977
You're kidding.

36
00:03:22,337 --> 00:03:24,697
I don't know if I have any tears left to cry.

37
00:03:25,217 --> 00:03:27,777
He already agreed, so it's not like we can back out now.

38
00:03:27,837 --> 00:03:30,717
I doubt he would go to the trouble if he didn't have something in mind.

39
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:32,877
Eh, I wouldn't be so sure about that.

40
00:03:32,877 --> 00:03:36,677
Well, unless he's thinking he can nab us a shipwreck from Foxy's crew.

41
00:03:38,637 --> 00:03:40,357
Screaming Hot Bombardment!

42
00:03:40,597 --> 00:03:41,757
Pirate Dodgeball!

43
00:03:45,477 --> 00:03:47,837
It's time for the second three-coin game!

44
00:03:48,077 --> 00:03:50,837
The events this time are a team-wide dodgeball showdown,

45
00:03:51,037 --> 00:03:52,957
a brutal new twist on a childhood favorite,

46
00:03:53,217 --> 00:03:55,097
and a one-on-one boxing beatdown!

47
00:03:55,377 --> 00:03:58,517
Like the previous game, each crew member can only participate twice!

48
00:03:58,737 --> 00:04:01,377
In other words, last-minute light-up changes will not be allowed!

49
00:04:01,377 --> 00:04:03,117
Oh, no two ways about it.

50
00:04:03,157 --> 00:04:04,817
This time, they're gonna pick me for sure.

51
00:04:05,097 --> 00:04:06,897
Yeah, right. I know they've got their eyes on me.

52
00:04:07,017 --> 00:04:09,757
I'm doomed to spend the rest of my life as their poster girl.

53
00:04:10,017 --> 00:04:11,297
Keep telling yourself that,

54
00:04:11,377 --> 00:04:13,277
but we don't want either of you on our crew.

55
00:04:13,457 --> 00:04:15,357
You're too scary, he's too weak.

56
00:04:15,657 --> 00:04:18,217
With our second Daveyback fight of the day about to start,

57
00:04:18,317 --> 00:04:21,477
I'm back in the announcer's seat to explain the rules of our first match.

58
00:04:22,097 --> 00:04:24,477
The name of the game is Hit and Deadball!

59
00:04:24,717 --> 00:04:27,597
The balls in question are the two you see on the field right now!

60
00:04:27,597 --> 00:04:29,957
If the opposing team hits you with one of those babies,

61
00:04:30,097 --> 00:04:31,037
you're out of the game!

62
00:04:31,377 --> 00:04:34,177
The teams are divided into on-court and off-court members!

63
00:04:34,657 --> 00:04:36,977
They're free to choose which ones go where and whatever number,

64
00:04:37,197 --> 00:04:38,737
but once you run out of on-court members,

65
00:04:38,837 --> 00:04:39,717
you lose the match!

66
00:04:40,137 --> 00:04:42,197
Keep in mind that although the off-court members

67
00:04:42,197 --> 00:04:44,257
can throw the ball around just like anyone else,

68
00:04:44,337 --> 00:04:46,977
they are not allowed to enter the court under any circumstance!

69
00:04:47,697 --> 00:04:49,037
They make it sound all fancy,

70
00:04:49,157 --> 00:04:51,337
but it seems like regular old dodgeball to me.

71
00:04:51,697 --> 00:04:53,537
There are some other miscellaneous details,

72
00:04:53,657 --> 00:04:55,297
so be sure to read the rulebook carefully!

73
00:04:55,297 --> 00:04:58,577
That's the rulebook?

74
00:04:58,577 --> 00:05:00,577
You wouldn't expect it to be so thick.

75
00:05:01,857 --> 00:05:03,757
Hit and Deadball is one of the greatest

76
00:05:03,757 --> 00:05:05,857
and most time-honored Davey back-fight games!

77
00:05:06,097 --> 00:05:08,037
Because it has been played so many times over the years,

78
00:05:08,137 --> 00:05:11,017
more and more rules have been added to balance and perfect its form!

79
00:05:11,317 --> 00:05:14,737
Only by strict adherence to these rules can the game truly be enjoyed!

80
00:05:14,737 --> 00:05:16,917
What's the point in preaching to us about the rules

81
00:05:16,917 --> 00:05:18,477
if you're going to break them all anyway?

82
00:05:18,797 --> 00:05:21,657
Did you just give us the rulebook so we'll know how bad you're cheating?

83
00:05:21,857 --> 00:05:22,977
No, no, no!

84
00:05:23,277 --> 00:05:25,157
Take a look at the first page, mademoiselle!

85
00:05:25,697 --> 00:05:26,777
Referee regulations.

86
00:05:27,337 --> 00:05:30,197
He who makes a judgment contrary to the rules written here

87
00:05:30,197 --> 00:05:31,617
shall be beheaded on the spot.

88
00:05:32,217 --> 00:05:33,297
Beheaded? Scary!

89
00:05:33,957 --> 00:05:35,317
And there you have it.

90
00:05:35,537 --> 00:05:39,577
On that topic, this game will be officiated by a team of five referees

91
00:05:39,577 --> 00:05:42,357
headed by a vet with 50 years of experience!

92
00:05:42,777 --> 00:05:43,537
Roku Roshi!

93
00:05:44,737 --> 00:05:47,257
With any luck, we might actually get a fair fight this time around.

94
00:05:48,057 --> 00:05:50,957
Team Foxy has a veritable armada of players!

95
00:05:51,397 --> 00:05:53,697
Truly a stupendous spectacle to see!

96
00:05:54,577 --> 00:05:58,477
Sadly, the Straw Hats pale in comparison with their diminutive showing.

97
00:05:58,857 --> 00:06:01,937
Sporting a measly seven members, I must wonder if they're even trying.

98
00:06:02,297 --> 00:06:03,537
Okay, we get it!

99
00:06:04,017 --> 00:06:05,457
Let's get this show on the road!

100
00:06:05,837 --> 00:06:08,077
We'll start the match off with the double opening tip!

101
00:06:09,797 --> 00:06:12,437
Each team bring two players to the center of the field!

102
00:06:14,737 --> 00:06:17,917
Hey, do you mind if I do this?

103
00:06:18,137 --> 00:06:18,297
Hmm?

104
00:06:19,117 --> 00:06:20,317
Yeah, be my guest.

105
00:06:20,617 --> 00:06:22,217
Go jump your heart out, little guy.

106
00:06:22,897 --> 00:06:23,437
Oh, right!

107
00:06:27,877 --> 00:06:29,177
Chopper has transformed!

108
00:06:29,437 --> 00:06:31,397
It looks like he's not just Fluff after all!

109
00:06:31,517 --> 00:06:33,977
He could turn out to be a powerful player for the Straw Hats!

110
00:06:33,977 --> 00:06:34,877
Oh, no!

111
00:06:35,097 --> 00:06:35,857
What's that?

112
00:06:36,117 --> 00:06:37,797
Now he's not cute at all!

113
00:06:38,377 --> 00:06:40,397
Ready, set, and go!

114
00:06:53,297 --> 00:06:54,217
Nice catch!

115
00:06:54,217 --> 00:06:56,097
Now give him a good spike to the face!

116
00:06:56,417 --> 00:06:57,757
Aim straight for Splithead!

117
00:06:57,897 --> 00:06:58,897
Come on, Chopper!

118
00:06:59,397 --> 00:07:00,397
Let's go!

119
00:07:02,357 --> 00:07:02,817
Wait!

120
00:07:05,137 --> 00:07:05,537
Shit!

121
00:07:06,997 --> 00:07:07,857
Oh, no!

122
00:07:08,097 --> 00:07:09,377
Our boss is in trouble!

123
00:07:15,057 --> 00:07:15,617
What?

124
00:07:15,877 --> 00:07:17,457
He's already out of the game?

125
00:07:17,457 --> 00:07:19,897
Yeah, you really showed their boss who's boss!

126
00:07:20,337 --> 00:07:20,777
Safe!

127
00:07:21,057 --> 00:07:21,497
Safe!

128
00:07:21,637 --> 00:07:22,557
What do you mean, safe?

129
00:07:22,617 --> 00:07:24,317
That was a clean hit, you old fart!

130
00:07:24,817 --> 00:07:26,777
It's a violation of Article 23!

131
00:07:27,237 --> 00:07:28,657
Blows to the face do not count!

132
00:07:28,857 --> 00:07:29,557
You're kidding!

133
00:07:31,557 --> 00:07:32,437
Now what?

134
00:07:32,797 --> 00:07:34,637
Well, boss, that looked like it hurt.

135
00:07:35,497 --> 00:07:36,757
Don't laugh, Hamburg.

136
00:07:36,857 --> 00:07:38,097
You're gonna make boss cry.

137
00:07:40,637 --> 00:07:42,037
Get them while they're distracted!

138
00:07:42,037 --> 00:07:45,477
Give them a good one for me, Sanji!

139
00:07:45,817 --> 00:07:48,497
Yeah, I'll show them the power of our sweet love!

140
00:07:50,057 --> 00:07:51,137
Here they come!

141
00:07:51,397 --> 00:07:52,877
You might want to clear out of here!

142
00:08:01,097 --> 00:08:01,577
Hey!

143
00:08:02,117 --> 00:08:02,977
Take it easy!

144
00:08:03,057 --> 00:08:04,417
We're still warming up here!

145
00:08:12,037 --> 00:08:12,537
Hmph!

146
00:08:18,917 --> 00:08:23,097
Eighteen members of Team Foxy are hereby eliminated for getting knocked out of bounds!

147
00:08:23,177 --> 00:08:23,937
Way to go!

148
00:08:24,057 --> 00:08:25,777
What a shock from the Straw Hats!

149
00:08:25,997 --> 00:08:29,057
The Shep and the Swordsman both blew nine players right off the field!

150
00:08:29,317 --> 00:08:31,337
Damn, I thought I'd get more than you.

151
00:08:31,717 --> 00:08:33,157
Yeah, knock them dead, Sanji!

152
00:08:33,337 --> 00:08:34,297
Knock them dead, Zoro!

153
00:08:36,837 --> 00:08:37,717
Pardon me.

154
00:08:37,717 --> 00:08:42,537
Wow, do you think we could take out nine people, too?

155
00:08:43,177 --> 00:08:43,737
Nine?

156
00:08:43,857 --> 00:08:44,717
I'll do ten!

157
00:08:47,417 --> 00:08:48,977
Gum gum!

158
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:50,097
Slick shot!

159
00:08:58,537 --> 00:09:00,037
Out of bounds!

160
00:09:00,237 --> 00:09:02,497
Ten members from Team Foxy are eliminated!

161
00:09:02,857 --> 00:09:03,737
Oh, yeah!

162
00:09:04,197 --> 00:09:05,377
That's a new record!

163
00:09:05,377 --> 00:09:08,677
Yet another strong showing from the Straw Hats!

164
00:09:08,877 --> 00:09:12,097
They're thinning out the competition, but Team Foxy finally has them all!

165
00:09:12,717 --> 00:09:14,137
Let's see how many I can knock out!

166
00:09:14,157 --> 00:09:14,997
Go on, Chopper!

167
00:09:15,157 --> 00:09:15,997
Even the score!

168
00:09:16,177 --> 00:09:17,917
Nine, ten, eleven, or more!

169
00:09:18,037 --> 00:09:19,537
Sure, you got it!

170
00:09:22,537 --> 00:09:23,017
Ah!

