Ah!

195
00:09:35,357 --> 00:09:38,157
The last-minute catch from Hamburg saves the day!

196
00:09:38,157 --> 00:09:40,857
Now Team Foxy has both balls in their possession!

197
00:09:40,857 --> 00:09:43,077
Could it finally be time for a comeback?

198
00:09:43,077 --> 00:09:43,957
Poo-poo-poo!

199
00:09:43,957 --> 00:09:45,817
Nice work as always, Hamburg!

200
00:09:45,817 --> 00:09:47,917
Now why don't you pass those balls to Big Pan?

201
00:09:47,917 --> 00:09:49,037
Roger, boss!

202
00:09:51,537 --> 00:09:52,477
Right!

203
00:09:52,477 --> 00:09:53,657
This is it!

204
00:09:53,657 --> 00:09:55,577
Take them all out in one shot!

205
00:09:55,957 --> 00:09:56,957
Poo-poo-poo!

206
00:09:56,957 --> 00:09:57,617
boy!

207
00:09:57,617 --> 00:09:59,497
Yeah, do they do you okay?

208
00:10:00,037 --> 00:10:01,377
Good...

209
00:10:01,677 --> 00:10:02,457
Not me!

210
00:10:02,457 --> 00:10:06,837
Please, not me!

211
00:10:06,837 --> 00:10:10,137
I do not, man!

212
00:10:10,137 --> 00:10:20,917
What's up, no!

213
00:10:23,257 --> 00:10:25,257
What happened? I can't see!

214
00:10:26,357 --> 00:10:27,717
Out of bounds!

215
00:10:28,197 --> 00:10:32,637
Mr. Longnose and 22 members of Team Foxy are hereby eliminated!

216
00:10:35,237 --> 00:10:37,137
That looked bad. Are you okay?

217
00:10:37,417 --> 00:10:39,697
Yeah, it takes more than that to kill me.

218
00:10:40,137 --> 00:10:42,377
Hey, and look, I got the ball!

219
00:10:42,377 --> 00:10:47,017
Big Pan's devastating dodgeball smash eliminated the Straw Hat's Longnose Sniper,

220
00:10:47,017 --> 00:10:50,377
but caused a crushing amount of collateral damage to his own team.

221
00:10:50,377 --> 00:10:53,657
Now Foxy and Hamburg are the only ones left on the field.

222
00:10:53,657 --> 00:10:57,657
At this rate, the Foxy Pirates may be undone by their own strength.

223
00:10:58,457 --> 00:11:00,457
The match is now 2-4!

224
00:11:02,057 --> 00:11:03,417
What's next?

225
00:11:03,417 --> 00:11:05,337
Who will reign supreme?

226
00:11:10,137 --> 00:11:12,377
The Foxy Pirates

227
00:11:12,377 --> 00:11:14,377
The Foxy Pirates

228
00:11:14,377 --> 00:11:27,657
Hey, boss, what now?

229
00:11:27,657 --> 00:11:29,017
What do you mean, what now?

230
00:11:29,017 --> 00:11:32,457
I can't use my slow, slow beam as long as that archaeologist chick is here.

231
00:11:32,457 --> 00:11:35,097
So there's only one choice left.

232
00:11:35,737 --> 00:11:37,437
You mean you know what?

233
00:11:37,437 --> 00:11:38,797
P-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p .

234
00:11:38,797 --> 00:11:39,997
You know what, indeed.

235
00:11:40,697 --> 00:11:45,477
Forum

236
00:11:45,477 --> 00:11:49,177
What a turn of events!

237
00:11:49,177 --> 00:11:51,477
Now Hamburg is out of the game, too!

238
00:11:51,477 --> 00:11:54,477
Good one, Robin!

239
00:11:54,477 --> 00:11:56,477
Hamburg is safe!

240
00:11:56,477 --> 00:12:00,477
You sure? Article 54 states that while the face doesn't count,

241
00:12:00,477 --> 00:12:02,477
the top of the head is still fair game.

242
00:12:02,477 --> 00:12:06,477
If I were you, I'd start using my head first before somebody chops it off!

243
00:12:06,477 --> 00:12:08,477
The girl is right! Hamburg is out!

244
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:09,477
I'm sorry, sir!

245
00:12:09,477 --> 00:12:12,477
The Straw Hacks archaeologist has memorized the massive rulebook

246
00:12:12,477 --> 00:12:16,477
in only moments by flexing the mighty muscles of her mind!

247
00:12:16,477 --> 00:12:18,477
You read all that? Awesome!

248
00:12:18,477 --> 00:12:21,477
Thanks for the compliment, but I'm only about halfway through.

249
00:12:21,477 --> 00:12:25,477
Well, either way, they've only got one left, so let's finish them off quick!

250
00:12:25,477 --> 00:12:28,477
You got it.

251
00:12:28,477 --> 00:12:31,477
Hey, Sanji!

252
00:12:31,477 --> 00:12:33,477
Yes, ladies?

253
00:12:33,477 --> 00:12:38,477
Please don't hit our boss. Just give that ball to us, okay?

254
00:12:38,477 --> 00:12:40,477
Of course!

255
00:12:40,477 --> 00:12:42,477
You're so sweet!

256
00:12:42,477 --> 00:12:44,477
Now would you mind getting knocked out of the game?

257
00:12:44,477 --> 00:12:46,477
As a favor for me?

258
00:12:46,477 --> 00:12:52,477
Why, it would be my pleasure, ma'am! You can hit me wherever you like!

259
00:12:53,477 --> 00:12:55,477
If you don't get up, I'll knock you out!

260
00:12:55,477 --> 00:13:08,477
Oh, love hunter Sanji has been blissfully bludgeoned and endearingly eliminated from the game!

261
00:13:08,477 --> 00:13:11,477
Now he'll be joining his long-nosed companion on the sidelines!

262
00:13:11,477 --> 00:13:12,477
Bye-bye!

263
00:13:14,477 --> 00:13:15,477
You make me sick.

264
00:13:15,477 --> 00:13:16,477
We should've seen that coming.

265
00:13:16,477 --> 00:13:19,477
On the upside, their boss is the only one left.

266
00:13:19,477 --> 00:13:23,477
We can't celebrate yet. You never know what might happen until the very end.

267
00:13:24,477 --> 00:13:25,477
Yes, good point!

268
00:13:27,477 --> 00:13:29,477
Huh? No way!

269
00:13:29,477 --> 00:13:30,477
What the?

270
00:13:30,477 --> 00:13:36,477
There it is! Hidden Deadpool's top secret weapon finally makes an appearance!

271
00:13:36,477 --> 00:13:37,477
Say hello!

272
00:13:37,477 --> 00:13:40,477
Who the Mr. Accu-cannon?

273
00:13:40,477 --> 00:13:48,477
Hey, Raph, are you really gonna allow this? That thing is obviously against the rule!

274
00:13:48,477 --> 00:13:50,477
So that's Mr. Accu-cannon?

275
00:13:50,477 --> 00:13:54,477
Wait! Why are you acting like you know all about this doohickey? Did I miss something?

276
00:13:54,477 --> 00:13:59,477
I ran across an article about it in the rule book, but I hadn't actually seen the device until now.

277
00:13:59,477 --> 00:14:04,477
Rule number 322! The only weapon allowed is Mr. Accu-cannon!

278
00:14:04,477 --> 00:14:06,477
Why would you make a rule just for that dumb thing?

279
00:14:06,477 --> 00:14:08,477
I don't know! Seems pretty awesome to me!

280
00:14:08,477 --> 00:14:13,477
What's the point? Listen, I don't care how big your Mr. Cannon whatever is, you're still gonna lose!

281
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:15,477
I wouldn't be so sure!

282
00:14:15,477 --> 00:14:18,477
Hey, Porcha, you ready to finish him up?

283
00:14:18,477 --> 00:14:25,477
I thought you'd never ask, boss! Better not blink. Flower hypnosis, go!

284
00:14:25,477 --> 00:14:26,477
Not again!

285
00:14:26,477 --> 00:14:28,477
Hurry up and close your eyes!

286
00:14:28,477 --> 00:14:29,477
Oh!

287
00:14:29,477 --> 00:14:32,477
Can you play without dirty tricks for once?

288
00:14:32,477 --> 00:14:33,477
Now's your chance! Fire!

289
00:14:33,477 --> 00:14:37,477
Oh, I will! Like shooting fish in a barrel!

290
00:14:37,477 --> 00:14:42,477
I don't have to see, I can feel.

291
00:14:42,477 --> 00:14:49,477
Even without my swords, I'm still a swordsman.

292
00:14:49,477 --> 00:14:59,477
What power? The swordless swordsman not only sliced the ball in half with his bare hands, he did it with his eyes closed!

293
00:14:59,477 --> 00:15:00,477
Oh no!

294
00:15:00,477 --> 00:15:02,477
Zoro of Team Straw Hat is out!

295
00:15:02,477 --> 00:15:03,477
Why, what'd I do?

296
00:15:03,477 --> 00:15:04,477
Huh?

297
00:15:04,477 --> 00:15:11,477
Rule number 645. Even with hands, no slicing the ball. Rules also state Foxy gets a new ball!

298
00:15:11,477 --> 00:15:12,477
What?!

299
00:15:12,477 --> 00:15:15,477
Oh well, battle on next time!

300
00:15:15,477 --> 00:15:22,477
What a shame! It was an impressive move from Zoro, but the rules are the rules!

301
00:15:22,477 --> 00:15:27,477
Are you okay? I don't think he's taking this too well.

302
00:15:27,477 --> 00:15:28,477
Hey there, buddy!

303
00:15:28,477 --> 00:15:32,477
Whatever you're about to say, I don't want to hear it, especially after that stunt you just pulled.

304
00:15:32,477 --> 00:15:37,477
Whoa! The match is now 2 to 1! And Mr. Accu-Canon is ready to go!

305
00:15:37,477 --> 00:15:44,477
Time to pick up where I left off!

306
00:15:44,477 --> 00:15:46,477
Yeah? Then let's see what you've got!

307
00:15:48,477 --> 00:15:49,477
Bring it on!

308
00:15:49,477 --> 00:15:52,477
Ultra-fast level 5, go!

309
00:15:52,477 --> 00:15:55,477
Let's see you dodge this, you brats!

310
00:16:07,477 --> 00:16:14,477
No! Choppy!

311
00:16:14,477 --> 00:16:19,477
The doctor makes a noble sacrifice for his captain, but is this the end for him?

312
00:16:19,477 --> 00:16:23,477
Hey! They said hits to the face don't count, right?

313
00:16:23,477 --> 00:16:25,477
Was that his face?

314
00:16:25,477 --> 00:16:31,477
Huh! Now that you mention it, I'm not sure where that is exactly. With all that fluff, it's sorta hard to tell.

315
00:16:31,477 --> 00:16:32,477
He's so brave!

316
00:16:32,477 --> 00:16:37,477
Hey, ref, can't you see a pirates honor is at stake here? I'm telling you that was his face!

317
00:16:37,477 --> 00:16:42,477
That's right! Any real man knows to show some respect when a pirate takes one for the team!

318
00:16:42,477 --> 00:16:54,477
Hitting up face! Hitting up face! Hitting up face! Hitting up face! Hitting up face! Hitting up face! Hitting up face! Hitting up face! Hitting up face!

319
00:16:54,477 --> 00:17:00,477
If pirates honor is at stake, then the choice is obvious, is it? The ball hit him in the face! And blows to the face do not count!

320
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:02,477
Blows to the face do not count!

321
00:17:02,477 --> 00:17:04,477
You're the best!

322
00:17:04,477 --> 00:17:06,477
However...

323
00:17:08,477 --> 00:17:09,477
However?

324
00:17:09,477 --> 00:17:11,477
Even if blows to the face don't count,

325
00:17:11,477 --> 00:17:14,477
you're out of bounds, so you're still eliminated.

326
00:17:14,477 --> 00:17:16,477
Say it ain't so!

327
00:17:16,477 --> 00:17:19,477
This is a real tragedy!

328
00:17:19,477 --> 00:17:22,477
Even after the Riff acknowledged his captain saving face block,

329
00:17:22,477 --> 00:17:23,477
he's still out!

330
00:17:23,477 --> 00:17:26,477
The brave little doctor will surely be missed by all!

331
00:17:26,477 --> 00:17:29,477
Even so, he will be remembered as a true man of the sea!

332
00:17:30,477 --> 00:17:31,477
Choppy!

333
00:17:31,477 --> 00:17:34,477
Hey, you still hanging in there?

334
00:17:34,477 --> 00:17:36,477
Yeah, but it doesn't matter.

335
00:17:36,477 --> 00:17:38,477
I'm out of the game either way.

336
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:43,477
Don't worry. Leave the rest to me.

337
00:17:43,477 --> 00:17:46,477
Oh, and thanks, Chopper. Nice save.

338
00:17:46,477 --> 00:17:48,477
What makes you think I want to hear that?

339
00:17:48,477 --> 00:17:51,477
That doesn't make me happy at all, you big jerk!

340
00:17:53,477 --> 00:17:54,477
Not too bad, Choppy!

341
00:17:54,477 --> 00:17:57,477
I can't wait till I win and you're back on my crew!

342
00:17:57,477 --> 00:18:00,477
Gotta go through me first, Split-head!

343
00:18:01,477 --> 00:18:03,477
Both teams are backed up against the wall

344
00:18:03,477 --> 00:18:07,477
as our courageous captains face off in a climactic confrontation!

345
00:18:07,477 --> 00:18:08,477
Heep, heep, heep, heep, heep!

346
00:18:08,477 --> 00:18:10,477
I warn you, this is gonna hurt!

347
00:18:10,477 --> 00:18:12,477
I think I'd give up now if I were you!

348
00:18:13,477 --> 00:18:16,477
Huh! Why would I give up when you're the one who's gonna lose?

349
00:18:16,477 --> 00:18:18,477
I wouldn't be so sure about that!

350
00:18:18,477 --> 00:18:22,477
Why don't you take a good look around before you start spouting nonsense?

351
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:26,477
Here comes the Omnidirectional Sept!

352
00:18:27,477 --> 00:18:29,477
Say your prayers, Butterboy!

353
00:18:30,477 --> 00:18:31,477
What are they doing now?

354
00:18:31,477 --> 00:18:33,477
Hey, what's up with those balls, old man?

355
00:18:33,477 --> 00:18:35,477
That's gotta be against the rules!

356
00:18:35,477 --> 00:18:39,477
The rulebook clearly states that players can use as many fake balls as they like!

357
00:18:39,477 --> 00:18:41,477
You talk big, but you're just as bad as the last ref!

358
00:18:41,477 --> 00:18:45,477
Damn, unless we can get a ref of our own, we're never gonna see the end of this!

359
00:18:45,477 --> 00:18:47,477
Don't pay any attention to those guys, Luffy!

360
00:18:47,477 --> 00:18:50,477
You and Foxy are the only ones with a real ball!

361
00:18:50,477 --> 00:18:52,477
Just keep your eye on him!

362
00:18:52,477 --> 00:18:53,477
Oh, how did she know?

363
00:18:53,477 --> 00:18:54,477
What's wrong with this guy?

364
00:18:54,477 --> 00:18:57,477
I'm starting to think his brain is split too!

365
00:18:57,477 --> 00:19:01,477
They call me split brain, I swear I'm gonna cry!

366
00:19:01,477 --> 00:19:02,477
Sorry, pal.

367
00:19:02,477 --> 00:19:06,477
It looks like I'm gonna have to break your Mr. Whatchamacallit thing!

368
00:19:06,477 --> 00:19:08,477
It's tiny!

369
00:19:08,477 --> 00:19:10,477
There it goes!

370
00:19:10,477 --> 00:19:12,477
Hello.

371
00:19:12,477 --> 00:19:14,477
Hey, hey!

372
00:19:14,477 --> 00:19:15,477
Yeah!

373
00:19:15,477 --> 00:19:16,477
Hey!

374
00:19:16,477 --> 00:19:17,477
Hey!

375
00:19:17,477 --> 00:19:18,477
Hey!

376
00:19:18,477 --> 00:19:19,477
Hey!

377
00:19:19,477 --> 00:19:20,477
Hey!

378
00:19:20,477 --> 00:19:21,477
Hey!

379
00:19:21,477 --> 00:19:22,477
Hey!

380
00:19:22,477 --> 00:19:23,477
Hey!

381
00:19:23,477 --> 00:19:24,477
Hey!

382
00:19:24,477 --> 00:19:25,477
Oh my!

383
00:19:25,477 --> 00:19:26,477
Where'd this come from?

384
00:19:26,477 --> 00:19:29,477
Better watch where you stretch that arm!

385
00:19:29,477 --> 00:19:30,477
Come on, boys!

386
00:19:30,477 --> 00:19:32,477
Let's shuffle!

387
00:19:32,477 --> 00:19:44,517
Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! SHUFFLE TIME! SHUFFLE TIME! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time!

388
00:19:44,517 --> 00:19:49,197
This is bad! If he can't tell which ones are real and which ones are fake he won't be able to dodge!

389
00:19:49,197 --> 00:19:54,217
Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time! Shuffle Time!

390
00:19:56,297 --> 00:19:59,477
Alright Mr. Smart Guy! Do you know which balls are real now?

391
00:19:59,477 --> 00:20:01,877
Better figure it out fast, before they hit you!

392
00:20:01,877 --> 00:20:05,457
Shut up! I'll just catch all the balls and then it won't matter!

393
00:20:05,637 --> 00:20:07,457
Don't you get snarky with me, boy!

394
00:20:07,877 --> 00:20:10,337
Just sit back and accept your defeat with grace.

395
00:20:10,677 --> 00:20:12,797
Now, time to let those balls fly!

396
00:20:22,557 --> 00:20:26,117
Heh, nice try. But you're finished.

397
00:20:26,497 --> 00:20:27,937
Hey, look out behind you!

398
00:20:27,937 --> 00:20:32,857
Luffy, don't dodge! Let it hit your face!

399
00:20:32,937 --> 00:20:34,357
Right, easy for you to say.

400
00:20:39,277 --> 00:20:39,977
He did it!

401
00:20:44,857 --> 00:20:45,697
All right!

402
00:20:45,697 --> 00:20:46,537
Oh!

403
00:20:55,537 --> 00:20:58,077
Straw hat, Luffy! You're out!

404
00:20:58,537 --> 00:21:01,157
Why? I thought it didn't count if you got hit in the face!

405
00:21:01,697 --> 00:21:03,037
Rule 999.

406
00:21:03,577 --> 00:21:07,117
Interesting any part of the ball results in instant disqualification.

407
00:21:07,497 --> 00:21:09,897
Check the rulebook yourself if you don't believe me.

408
00:21:09,897 --> 00:21:14,737
Unfortunately, he's correct. It's on the very last page.

409
00:21:15,737 --> 00:21:16,237
What?

410
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:18,697
Why does that rule even exist?

411
00:21:23,697 --> 00:21:24,857
It's over!

412
00:21:25,237 --> 00:21:31,237
Straw hat, Luffy has hit his way to defeat as Team Foxy claims victory in the first round!

413
00:21:32,657 --> 00:21:34,237
Not again!

414
00:21:39,897 --> 00:21:46,817
...

415
00:21:47,137 --> 00:21:50,897
...

416
00:21:51,697 --> 00:21:52,557
...

417
00:21:52,557 --> 00:21:54,777
...

418
00:21:54,777 --> 00:21:57,477
...

419
00:21:58,277 --> 00:22:01,237
...

420
00:22:01,237 --> 00:22:07,597
...

421
00:22:07,597 --> 00:22:08,357
...

422
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:10,151
Warpiece! Showdown on the cliff! Red light, green light!

423
00:23:10,151 --> 00:23:12,151
Huh? Did Zoro get lost again?

